      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Spot ETF custody concentrates Bitcoin and Ethereum holdings at a small number of TradFi custodians and issuers, recreating single-point-of-failure exposure that on-chain self-custody was designed to eliminate.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "SEC approval has been asset-specific and politically contingent — Gensler explicitly stated BTC ETF approval does not extend to other assets, leaving Solana, XRP, and dozens of altcoin ETF filings in legal limbo.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Ethereum spot ETFs recorded a four-day outflow streak with Grayscale's GBTC-style rotation pattern repeating, showing that early inflows can rapidly reverse when investors arbitrage trust-to-ETF fee differentials.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "ETF inflow and outflow cycles have become a reflexive price driver — single-day $263M inflow events correlate with Bitcoin surging past key price levels, compressing the independence between product mechanics and spot market moves.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Slashing / Staking penalty",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Proposed spot Ether staking ETFs risk concentrating validator stake under a handful of ETF issuers, and S&P Global warned this would heighten Ethereum's validator concentration risk at the protocol level.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "Spot Bitcoin and Ethereum ETFs hold underlying assets in custodied cold storage rather than on-chain smart contracts, so direct smart-contract exploit risk is minimal for current approved products.",
          "source": ""
        }
